      "timestamp": "2026-05-28T18:52:38.878Z",
      "type": "message",
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The problem is clear. The product page calls `getInventory()` (which uses `connection()` to force dynamic, runtime data) at the top level of the page component. Because the whole page `await`s that data before rendering, nothing — including the static title \"Premium Widget\" — appears until the dynamic inventory resolves.\n\nThe fix is to isolate the dynamic data fetch in its own component wrapped in `<Suspense>`, so the static shell (the title) renders/streams immediately while the inventory streams in afterward.",
