              "text": "Typechecks clean. Here's what I changed and why:\n\n**The problem:** `app/product/page.tsx` was an `async` component that called `await getInventory()` at the top level. `getInventory()` calls `connection()`, which forces dynamic rendering at request time. Because the entire page awaited that data before returning any markup, the browser saw nothing — including the static `<h1>Premium Widget</h1>` — until the inventory finished resolving.\n\n**The fix:** I moved the dynamic data fetch into its own `Inventory` component and wrapped it in a `<Suspense>` boundary. Now:\n\n- `ProductPage` is no longer `async` and awaits nothing, so its static shell — the title — is sent/rendered immediately.\n- The `connection()`-gated inventory streams in behind the Suspense boundary, showing a `Loading…` fallback until it resolves.\n\nThe title appears instantly while the stock/price stream in. The data behavior is unchanged.\n\nIf you'd also like the navigation itself to feel instant (route transition before the shell paints), the next step would be adding `app/product/loading.tsx`, but the Suspense change addresses the title-appears-immediately request directly."
